36. Epistemic Discipline

The framework adopts four labels throughout all versions:

· [V] Validated externally — A quantitative value directly reported by a cited source under specified experimental conditions.
· [R] Reported — A qualitative or quantitative observation documented in the literature but requiring contextual interpretation.
· [H] Hypothesis — A proposed mechanism not yet experimentally tested by ITO.
· [N] Not reported — The relevant literature does not provide the required measurement.

If a paper does not report $C_{\text{memory}}$, ITO writes:

\boxed{\text{NR}}

not $0$. Absence of measurement is not evidence of zero cost. NR is not imputed in the optimization layer.

---

37. Conclusion

The first five architectural tests provide preliminary evidence that an operation-based representation can unify systems that differ substantially in retrieval mechanism and control structure.

· BM25 establishes lexical retrieval as a minimal reference.
· Naive RAG demonstrates the basic retrieval-to-generation trajectory.
· Self-RAG introduces conditional retrieval, reflection, and adaptive control.
· DPR reveals that dense retrieval must be decomposed into query encoding, document encoding, and similarity search, while demonstrating that index configuration can radically alter the temporal and multidimensional cost profile of the same retrieval family.
· ColBERT provides the strongest refinement so far. It demonstrates that late interaction is not adequately represented as a single operation. Token-level representation, storage, MaxSim interaction, and token pruning have different computational roles and costs. MaxSim belongs to the retrieval mechanism rather than conventional post-retrieval reranking. Token pruning and context compression share a higher-level information-preservation principle while remaining architecturally distinct.

The resulting framework is therefore not yet a finished optimisation theory. It is a measurement architecture for constructing one.

The next stage is to challenge the current taxonomy with graph-based retrieval and adaptive multi-step systems. If GraphRAG / HippoRAG / LineageRAG and TASR / S2G-RAG reveal further stable primitives, the taxonomy can then be frozen temporarily and subjected to controlled ablation experiments.

Only after those measurements should ITO move toward a trajectory-level decision model such as a constrained MDP or POMDP.

The central scientific question remains:

\boxed{\text{How little computation is sufficient to obtain the information required for a reliable decision?}}

That is the real object ITO is trying to measure.

