Appendix D: Quality Metrics — INFOF1 and CITEF1

This appendix defines the subclaim-level metrics INFOF1 and CITEF1 adopted in §27.1, following the MiRAGE evaluation framework.

D.1 INFOF1 — Information Coverage and Factuality

Definition. INFOF1 is an F1 score over the information coverage of reference subclaims  R  by predicted subclaims  P :

\text{INFOF1} = \frac{2 \cdot \text{INFO}_P \cdot \text{INFO}_R}{\text{INFO}_P + \text{INFO}_R}

where:

·  \text{INFO}_P  = proportion of predicted subclaims  P  that are attested in  R  (precision),
·  \text{INFO}_R  = proportion of reference subclaims  R  that are attested in  P  (recall).

Interpretation. INFOF1 assesses factuality and information coverage at the subclaim level. A high INFOF1 indicates that the prediction both covers the reference information and does not introduce unsupported claims.

Recommendation. When reporting INFOF1, always report precision and recall separately, as the F1 is derived.

D.2 CITEF1 — Citation Quality

Definition. CITEF1 is an F1 score over citation support and citation attribution:

\text{CITEF1} = \frac{2 \cdot \text{CITE}_P \cdot \text{CITE}_R}{\text{CITE}_P + \text{CITE}_R}

where:

·  \text{CITE}_P  = proportion of subclaims supported by their cited sources (citation precision),
·  \text{CITE}_R  = proportion of subclaims that properly attribute their sources (citation recall).

Interpretation. CITEF1 assesses citation support and completeness at the subclaim level. A high CITEF1 indicates that citations are both accurate (cited sources support their associated subclaims) and complete (recalled information is properly attributed).

D.3 Comparison with Existing Metrics

Metric Granularity Alignment with human judgments
ROUGE Surface-level Low
BERTScore Surface-level Low
INFOF1 Subclaim-level High (validated)
CITEF1 Subclaim-level High (validated)
ALCE Citation Quality Sentence-level Low
ARGUE Sentence Support Sentence-level Low

The MiRAGE framework demonstrates that CITEF1 has the highest agreement with human judgments for both quality and grounding, validating the benefits of subclaim decomposition in support judgments.

D.4 Recommended Reporting Protocol

For quick diagnostics or compute-constrained settings, report ROUGE, BERTScore, INFOF1 (reference-based), and CITEF1 (reference-based). For comprehensive evaluation, report ROUGE, BERTScore, INFOF1 (source-based), CITEF1 (source-based), and RAGAS Faithfulness.

