Appendix E: Proposed Experimental Protocol

This appendix details the controlled ablation protocol proposed in §32. No experiments have been conducted. The protocol is specified for future execution.

E.1 Baseline and Augmentation

For a selected architecture, define  B =  minimal baseline. Progressively add operations:

B + O_i, \qquad B + O_i + O_j, \qquad \ldots

Measure:

\Delta Q = Q_{\text{augmented}} - Q_{\text{baseline}}, \qquad \Delta \mathbf{C} = \mathbf{C}_{\text{augmented}} - \mathbf{C}_{\text{baseline}}.

E.2 Quality–Cost Response Vector

The resulting empirical quantity is:

\boldsymbol{\eta}_i = \frac{\Delta Q}{\Delta \mathbf{C}}

Vector division is not mathematically defined in the ordinary scalar sense.  \boldsymbol{\eta}_i  should be represented as a quality–cost response vector, or converted into a scalar only after deployment weights are explicitly specified.

E.3 Query Stratification

Queries should be stratified by:

Stratum Dimension Rationale
Single-hop vs. multi-hop Query complexity Adaptive retrieval literature shows that indiscriminate fixed retrieval is suboptimal
Lexical vs. semantic Query type Different retrieval mechanisms excel on different query types
Short vs. long Query length Token budget and retrieval behaviour differ

E.4 Protocol Specifications

Element Specification
Dataset NQ, MS MARCO, HotpotQA
Query set size ≥ 1,000 queries per configuration
Retrieval metric Recall@ k , nDCG@10
Answer metric EM, F1, INFOF1, CITEF1
Hardware Fixed GPU and CPU configuration per run
Statistical test Paired bootstrap,  \alpha = 0.05 
Runs ≥ 3 seeds per configuration
Cost measurement Hardware profiler + wall-clock + tokenizer + memory profiler

E.5 First Controlled Retrieval Experiment

For dense RAG:

· Configuration A:  O_7 + O_{24} 
· Configuration B:  O_7 + O_{31} + O_{24} 
· Configuration C:  O_7 + O_{12} + O_{24} 
· Configuration D:  O_7 + O_{30} + O_{24} 
· Configuration E:  O_7 + O_{30} + O_{31} + O_{24} 

The experiment tests whether candidate selection, reranking, and retrieval gating produce independently measurable marginal benefits. The key measurement is not "which system wins?" It is:

\boxed{\text{What quality gain does each added operation buy, at what multidimensional cost?}}

