Appendix G: Epistemic Labels

The framework adopts four labels throughout all versions:

Label Definition Example
[V] Validated externally A quantitative value directly reported by a cited source under specified experimental conditions DPR index size = 64 GB on 21M documents
[R] Reported A qualitative or quantitative observation documented in the literature but requiring contextual interpretation ColBERT token pruning up to ~30% on MS MARCO
[H] Hypothesis A proposed mechanism not yet experimentally tested by ITO  O_{31}  Candidate Selection as an independent primitive
[N] Not reported The relevant literature does not provide the required measurement  C_{\text{memory}}  for a specific operation

G.1 NR ≠ 0 Convention

If a publication does not report a specific cost dimension, ITO records:

\boxed{\text{NR}}

not  0 . Absence of measurement is not evidence of zero cost. NR is not imputed in the optimization layer.

G.2 Application to Optimization

If a cost dimension is NR for an operation, that operation cannot be selected for deployment in contexts where that dimension is constrained. NR is not imputed. This rule preserves epistemic discipline in the optimization layer.

