J.13 Pareto Frontier in Quality–Cost Space

```
   Quality  Q
      ▲
      │
      │                                          ● p_full (reference)
      │                                       ╱
      │                                    ╱
      │                                 ╱
      │                              ╱
      │                           ╱
      │                        ╱   ← Pareto frontier
      │                     ╱        (non-dominated trajectories)
      │                  ╱
      │               ╱
      │            ╱
      │         ╱
      │      ╱  ← feasible region
      │   ╱
      │╱
      └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────► Cost  C

   Definition:

      P*(q) = { p ∈ P(q) | Q(p) ⪰ τ,
                ∄ p' : C(p') ⪯ C(p) with at least one strict inequality }

   A deployment selects p* ∈ P*(q) by scalarizing:

      C_w = w_c C_compute + w_l C_latency + w_t C_tokens
          + w_m C_memory + w_n C_network + w_a C_calls

   No universal justification for  w_latency = w_memory  or any equivalence.
```

